monolith softs Xenoblade Chronicles X is  basically the same as its predecessor  Xenoblade Chronicles except it's bigger  unbelievably bigger it's out this month  in Japan but North America isn't getting  it until later this year X is open world  is a welcomed experience for those of us  who are tired of the rigid hallway  formulas favored by many RPGs in the  past decade  you can walk literally anywhere within  the game's five continents on foot and  you can climb on pretty much anything  there are large structures made out of  rock and stone and with the right angle  jumps you can get all the way up to the  top there's never a dull moment in X  because you'll find that the areas  you're in are littered with crafting  materials and roaming monsters something  I love about Xenoblade Chronicles X is  its navigation the Wii U gamepad  displays a world map of sorts with a  couple of kind of strange tweaks rather  than your typical geographical layout  the map is a bunch of diamonds with  icons in them showing what landmarks are  in that area some of these icons  indicate checkpoints which are unlocked  by discovering new areas and then  setting down a beacon if you're killed  in battle any time after unlocking this  checkpoint  you'll be sent back to it until you find  a new one the most helpful tool is the  navigation ball it's a camera that you  can shoot straight into the air for a  bird's-eye view of everything you get  this very large swath of land and you  get to take in your surroundings you can  see monsters around corners and faraway  landmarks it's actually really beautiful  you get a very nice view of the world  that you're running around in combat is  basically the same as the last game the  arts are back which are special physical  and magical attacks but now encina Blade  Chronicles X you can wield a gun and a  weapon and there are special arts for  each speaking of combat enemy levels  don't scale to yours the monsters you  encounter will always be the same level  you can usually go after enemies two or  three levels above yours but not much  more any higher than that and you're  just asking for it on the surface level  Xenoblade Chronicles X is just more of  Xenoblade Chronicles same combat layout  in tone  but X builds on these ideas making them  larger and more complex based on what  we've seen it's a welcome addition to  our PG fans libraries and the Wii U  library as well  [Music]
 

